  <diagram id="page-1" name="Mapping from the conceptual model">
    <mxGraphModel grid="1" gridSize="10" page="1" pageWidth="2000" pageHeight="1270">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="title" parent="1" vertex="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=28;fontColor=#000000;spacing=0;" value="Mapping from the conceptual model">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="30" width="1850" height="70" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="notes" parent="1" vertex="1" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=16;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=16;fontColor=#000000;" value="&lt;table style=&quot;width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:16px&quot;&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Conceptual information&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Relational representation&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Account and roles&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;account&lt;/code&gt; stores shared facts. &lt;code&gt;resident&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;volunteer&lt;/code&gt; use its key as both PK and FK. Membership is overlapping and total: every account has one or both roles (BR1).&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Preferred postal codes&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;volunteer_preferred_postal_code&lt;/code&gt; has one row per volunteer/code pair, with no repeated codes and at most three per volunteer (BR9).&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Resident owns a request&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;pickup_request.terms_acceptance_id&lt;/code&gt; identifies the request-creation acceptance and its resident account. Q4 can share that acceptance across several item requests. Ownership is obtained through this required relationship (BR13, BR43).&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Request address and item&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Each request stores one category, quantity, historical estimated weight and pickup-address snapshot. The category reference supplies its description and current standard weight (BR30–BR35).&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Windows and status history&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Window rows contain individual Calgary slots. &lt;code&gt;status_change&lt;/code&gt; uses &lt;code&gt;(pickup_request_id, changed_at)&lt;/code&gt; for append-only history. A request starts Open (BR16–BR18, BR32, BR36).&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Assignment participation&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;The selected window identifies the request. The volunteer-acceptance row identifies the volunteer. &lt;code&gt;assignment&lt;/code&gt; stores its own acceptance, collection and ending facts (BR19–BR29).&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Delivery and facilities&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;delivery&lt;/code&gt; has unique assignment and evidence-photo references. &lt;code&gt;facility_accepts&lt;/code&gt; maps the facility/category relationship (BR25–BR28).&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Award earned through a role&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;ecopoints_award&lt;/code&gt; stores assignment, points and the formula used. Exactly one of &lt;code&gt;resident_award&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;code&gt;volunteer_award&lt;/code&gt; contains its key. The corresponding actor is derived through the assignment (BR11, BR41, BR55).&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Notification source&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Exactly one of &lt;code&gt;request_notification&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;code&gt;award_notification&lt;/code&gt; contains each notification key. Request notifications store their recipient. Award notifications derive their recipient through the award (BR10, BR48).&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Event metadata&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;request_event&lt;/code&gt; stores request sequence and action identity. &lt;code&gt;request_update_event&lt;/code&gt; stores the update reason. &lt;code&gt;request_changed_field&lt;/code&gt; stores one changed field per row. Notifications reference their event (BR58, BR61).&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Photos&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;photo.file_id&lt;/code&gt; is the ImageKit key. Requests may share an item photo after rescheduling. One delivery has one unique evidence photo, and item and evidence use are exclusive (BR51, BR60).&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Terms and subscriptions&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Each acceptance identifies one account, document, action and time. Each subscription endpoint identifies one browser subscription (BR2, BR29, BR38, BR40, BR43, BR54).&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Rescheduling&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;A nullable unique predecessor reference links a replacement request to one Missed request. Each predecessor has at most one replacement (BR50).&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="140" width="1900" height="1100" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
  <diagram id="page-2" name="Nullability and candidate keys">
    <mxGraphModel grid="1" gridSize="10" page="1" pageWidth="2000" pageHeight="770">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="title" parent="1" vertex="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=28;fontColor=#000000;spacing=0;" value="Nullability and candidate keys">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="30" width="1850" height="70" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="notes" parent="1" vertex="1" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=16;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=16;fontColor=#000000;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;line-height:1.45;margin:9px 0&quot;&gt;Nullable attributes are &lt;code&gt;account.deactivated_at&lt;/code&gt;; &lt;code&gt;push_subscription.expiration_time&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;user_agent&lt;/code&gt;; &lt;code&gt;pickup_request.notes&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;file_id&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;rescheduled_from_request_id&lt;/code&gt;; &lt;code&gt;status_change.reason&lt;/code&gt;; &lt;code&gt;assignment.collected_at&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;ended_at&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;end_reason&lt;/code&gt;; &lt;code&gt;recycling_facility.special_instructions&lt;/code&gt;; and &lt;code&gt;notification.pushed_at&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;line-height:1.45;margin:9px 0&quot;&gt;All primary keys are candidate keys. &lt;code&gt;delivery.assignment_id&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;delivery.file_id&lt;/code&gt; are additional candidate keys because each is required and unique. Both attributes of &lt;code&gt;award_notification&lt;/code&gt; are candidate keys for the same reason. The nullable unique predecessor reference identifies a replacement only within the non-null subset, so it is not a candidate key for the whole request relation. Partial active-slot uniqueness also does not identify historical window rows globally.&lt;/p&gt;">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="140" width="1900" height="600" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
  <diagram id="page-3" name="Value constraints">
    <mxGraphModel grid="1" gridSize="10" page="1" pageWidth="2000" pageHeight="1920">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="title" parent="1" vertex="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=28;fontColor=#000000;spacing=0;" value="Value constraints">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="30" width="1850" height="70" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="notes" parent="1" vertex="1" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=16;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=16;fontColor=#000000;" value="&lt;table style=&quot;width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:16px&quot;&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Attributes&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Domain&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Account IDs&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;3–50 lowercase characters from &lt;code&gt;a-z&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;0-9&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;_&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;-&lt;/code&gt;; immutable username and Firebase UID. Email is held by Firebase (BR3, BR56).&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Required names, IDs and file paths&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Non-empty text.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Postal codes&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Six uppercase Canadian letter/digit characters with no space. Application validation checks the Calgary address (BR7).&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Date of birth&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;At least 18 at registration; birth date cannot be in the future (BR6).&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Quantity and weights&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Positive integer quantity; positive exact standard and historical estimated weights. The system calculates the estimate at creation/edit (BR30–BR31).&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;start_hour&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Integer 0–23. Dates and hours are stored as Calgary local calendar values (BR32).&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Request/event sequences&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Positive BIGINT. &lt;code&gt;pickup_request.request_seq&lt;/code&gt; tracks the latest published event. &lt;code&gt;request_event.request_seq&lt;/code&gt; is the historical sequence for the referenced event (BR61).&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Status&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;Open&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;Assigned&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;Collected&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;Delivered&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;Cancelled&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;Expired&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;Missed&lt;/code&gt; (BR18).&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;End reason&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;Delivered&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;Resident_Cancelled&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;Volunteer_Cancelled&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;Missed_Pickup&lt;/code&gt; (BR23).&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Terms type&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;AT_RESIDENT_REGISTRATION_OR_ACTIVATION&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;AT_VOLUNTEER_REGISTRATION_OR_ACTIVATION&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;AT_RESIDENT_REQUEST_CREATION&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;AT_VOLUNTEER_ACCEPTANCE&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Update reason&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;edited&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;code&gt;reopened&lt;/code&gt;, from the RequestUpdated event.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Changed field&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;category&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;quantity&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;notes&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;windows&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;code&gt;photo&lt;/code&gt;; rows occur only for an &lt;code&gt;edited&lt;/code&gt; update.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Points and formula&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Positive exact &lt;code&gt;NUMERIC(23,2)&lt;/code&gt; points and the formula text used at award creation. Volunteer points are &lt;code&gt;3 * quantity + 4 * estimated_weight_kg&lt;/code&gt;; resident points are half that amount (BR41).&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Booleans&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Required &lt;code&gt;is_active&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;is_read&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;is_expired&lt;/code&gt; values.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;line-height:1.45;margin:9px 0&quot;&gt;The request estimate uses &lt;code&gt;NUMERIC(22,2)&lt;/code&gt; to accommodate an integer quantity multiplied by a &lt;code&gt;NUMERIC(10,2)&lt;/code&gt; unit weight. Points use &lt;code&gt;NUMERIC(23,2)&lt;/code&gt; to accommodate the reward formula while retaining exact decimals.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;line-height:1.45;margin:9px 0&quot;&gt;Notification type uses the closed list in contract section 13.1:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;pre style=&quot;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;REQUEST_CREATED&#10;NEW_MATCHING_REQUEST&#10;REQUEST_UPDATED_RESIDENT&#10;REQUEST_ASSIGNED_RESIDENT&#10;REQUEST_ASSIGNED_VOLUNTEER&#10;REQUEST_COLLECTED_RESIDENT&#10;REQUEST_COLLECTED_VOLUNTEER&#10;REQUEST_DELIVERED_RESIDENT&#10;REQUEST_DELIVERED_VOLUNTEER&#10;ASSIGNMENT_CANCELLED_BY_RESIDENT_RESIDENT&#10;ASSIGNMENT_CANCELLED_BY_RESIDENT_VOLUNTEER&#10;ASSIGNMENT_CANCELLED_BY_VOLUNTEER_RESIDENT&#10;ASSIGNMENT_CANCELLED_BY_VOLUNTEER_VOLUNTEER&#10;ASSIGNMENT_MISSED_RESIDENT&#10;ASSIGNMENT_MISSED_VOLUNTEER&#10;REQUEST_CANCELLED_RESIDENT&#10;REQUEST_EXPIRED_RESIDENT&#10;ECOPOINTS_AWARDED_ON_DELIVERY_RESIDENT&#10;ECOPOINTS_AWARDED_ON_DELIVERY_VOLUNTEER&#10;ECOPOINTS_AWARDED_ON_ASSIGNMENT_CANCELLATION_VOLUNTEER&#10;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;font-size:21px;font-weight:bold;margin-top:18px&quot;&gt;Reference categories&lt;/p&gt;&lt;table style=&quot;width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:16px&quot;&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Category ID&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Name&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Waste type&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Standard weight (kg)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;laptops&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Computers/Laptops&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Computers&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;2.50&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;desktops&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Computers/Desktops&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Computers&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;8.00&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;monitors&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Monitors&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Displays&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;5.00&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;tvs&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Televisions&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Displays&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;12.00&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;phones&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Phones&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Mobile Devices&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;0.20&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;tablets&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Tablets&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Mobile Devices&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;0.50&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;printers&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Printers&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Printers&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;6.00&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;small-appliances&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Small Appliances&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Small Appliances&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;3.00&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;cables-chargers&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Cables and Chargers&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Accessories&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;0.30&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="140" width="1900" height="1750" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
  <diagram id="page-4" name="Relationship and uniqueness constraints">
    <mxGraphModel grid="1" gridSize="10" page="1" pageWidth="2000" pageHeight="1370">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="title" parent="1" vertex="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=28;fontColor=#000000;spacing=0;" value="Relationship and uniqueness constraints">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="30" width="1850" height="70" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="notes" parent="1" vertex="1" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=16;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=16;fontColor=#000000;" value="&lt;table style=&quot;width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:16px&quot;&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Rule&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Required enforcement&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Total account specialization&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Every account has a resident row, a volunteer row or both. Serialize role changes on the account row and check the final state (BR1).&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Preferred-code limit&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Composite PK prevents duplicates. In a transaction, lock the volunteer row with &lt;code&gt;SELECT ... FOR UPDATE&lt;/code&gt;, then check that the resulting list has at most three postal codes (BR9).&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Request and assignment actors&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;In the insertion transaction, check that a request uses its resident&amp;#x27;s request-creation acceptance and an assignment uses its volunteer&amp;#x27;s acceptance. Check the account role, acceptance type and current terms document. Actor and acceptance links remain unchanged (BR29, BR38, BR43, BR54).&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Request history&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Each request has its initial Open entry. Later entries append in time order and are retained (BR16–BR18).&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Active pickup slots&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;In a transaction, lock the request row with &lt;code&gt;SELECT ... FOR UPDATE&lt;/code&gt;, then require one to three active windows and no duplicate &lt;code&gt;(pickup_request_id, pickup_date, start_hour)&lt;/code&gt; among them. Each new window starts in the future and ends within 30 days of the original creation time (BR32–BR36).&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Window history&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Retain replaced windows as inactive. Assignments retain their selected window reference (BR36).&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;One unfinished assignment per request&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;In the Q11 transaction, first lock the request row with &lt;code&gt;SELECT ... FOR UPDATE&lt;/code&gt;. Find its assignments through &lt;code&gt;pickup_window&lt;/code&gt; and reject a new assignment if any has &lt;code&gt;ended_at IS NULL&lt;/code&gt; (BR20).&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Assignment ending&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Ending fields are null together or set together. Collection follows acceptance; ending follows acceptance and collection. A Delivered ending requires collection and one delivery (BR21–BR26).&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Delivery&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Unique assignment and evidence photo; the facility accepts the request&amp;#x27;s category. Use a transaction for assignment ending and delivery insertion (BR25–BR28, BR44).&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Award role&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Insert the award and exactly one &lt;code&gt;resident_award&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;code&gt;volunteer_award&lt;/code&gt; row in the same transaction. Insert the processed-event ID first; its primary key rejects repeat processing. Check at most one award per assignment and role in this transaction. Self-delivery creates one award per role; eligible resident cancellation creates only a volunteer award, excluding self-cancellation (BR11, BR55).&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Notification source&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Insert the notification and exactly one &lt;code&gt;request_notification&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;code&gt;award_notification&lt;/code&gt; row in the same transaction, checking that its type matches the source. The required unique award FK allows at most one notification per award (BR48).&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Event identity&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;(pickup_request_id, request_seq)&lt;/code&gt; identifies an event. &lt;code&gt;transition_id&lt;/code&gt; is not unique: cancellation/reopening and missed/rescheduled pairs share an action ID (contract 10.2).&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Event details&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;An update-event subtype has reason &lt;code&gt;edited&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;code&gt;reopened&lt;/code&gt;. Its changed-field rows are distinct and permitted only for &lt;code&gt;edited&lt;/code&gt;. Request notifications reference the whole event key (BR58).&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Photos&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Item photos may be shared by requests after rescheduling. In the transaction that attaches a photo, lock its row with &lt;code&gt;SELECT ... FOR UPDATE&lt;/code&gt; and check that it is not used by both a delivery and a request (BR51, BR60).&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Rescheduling&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Predecessor reference is unique when present, is not self-referential, belongs to the same owner and points to a Missed request. At creation, copy the category, quantity, notes and photo; recalculate the estimate using the current category weight; and record new terms, windows, address and creation time. Later Open edits follow the normal rules (BR50; contract 12.5).&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Deactivation and history&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #b9a76c;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Apply active-work guards; retain historical requests, assignments and awards. Remove the account&amp;#x27;s notifications and subscriptions as specified (BR40, BR42, BR47, BR53).&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;line-height:1.45;margin:9px 0&quot;&gt;Rules involving several rows are checked in a transaction. Lock the relevant parent row with &lt;code&gt;SELECT ... FOR UPDATE&lt;/code&gt; before reading and changing related rows. Use the lecture SQL features and transactions for these checks; do not rely on database triggers or partial indexes.&lt;/p&gt;">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="140" width="1900" height="1600" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
  <diagram id="page-5" name="Derived data and implementation">
    <mxGraphModel grid="1" gridSize="10" page="1" pageWidth="2000" pageHeight="1070">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="title" parent="1" vertex="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=28;fontColor=#000000;spacing=0;" value="Derived data and implementation">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="30" width="1850" height="70" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="notes" parent="1" vertex="1" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=16;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=16;fontColor=#000000;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;line-height:1.45;margin:9px 0&quot;&gt;The normalized read paths are:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:8px 0&quot;&gt;• Request owner: &lt;code&gt;pickup_request → terms_acceptance.account_id&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:8px 0&quot;&gt;• Assignment request: &lt;code&gt;assignment → pickup_window.pickup_request_id&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:8px 0&quot;&gt;• Assignment volunteer: &lt;code&gt;assignment → terms_acceptance.account_id&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:8px 0&quot;&gt;• Award role: membership in &lt;code&gt;resident_award&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;code&gt;volunteer_award&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:8px 0&quot;&gt;• Resident award recipient: award → assignment → window → request → request acceptance → account.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:8px 0&quot;&gt;• Volunteer award recipient: award → assignment → volunteer acceptance → account.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:8px 0&quot;&gt;• Request notification recipient: &lt;code&gt;request_notification.account_id&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:8px 0&quot;&gt;• Award notification recipient: award notification → award → role-specific recipient path.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:8px 0&quot;&gt;• Request notification metadata: its event&amp;#x27;s request sequence and transition ID, optional update reason, and the changed-field rows. Services can assemble the response metadata object from these scalar relations.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;line-height:1.45;margin:9px 0&quot;&gt;Request status, assignment status, request expiry, delivery time, award kind/time, EcoPoints totals, eligible facilities and notification title/body continue to be derived from their documented source facts (BR12, BR24, BR33, BR44–BR45, BR57–BR59). Historical pickup addresses, estimates and award formulas retain their time-specific meaning.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;font-size:21px;font-weight:bold;margin-top:18px&quot;&gt;Physical implementation&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;line-height:1.45;margin:9px 0&quot;&gt;The SQL implementation must follow this 25-relation mapping, including its keys, domains and cross-row constraints. Service joins, seed scripts, operations and tests must use the same relations. Contract section 8 identifies the User, Request, Reward and Notification readers. Compatibility views or service projections can supply their API fields from the normalized relations.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;line-height:1.45;margin:9px 0&quot;&gt;The Notification Service owns the event/detail/source relations that store its consumed event facts. Request Service publishes the request sequences and transition IDs used by these relations. Event consumption may lag behind publication or arrive out of order. Stored event sequences can have gaps and need not yet reach the request&#x27;s latest published sequence.&lt;/p&gt;">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="140" width="1900" height="900" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>